    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by the elite efficiency of **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an 83.29 rating. His matchup against Montero provides the optimal blend of a favorable pitcher matchup and an ideal position in the three-hole, making him the anchor of our offensive output. **Luis Robert Jr.** also presents a high-ceiling opportunity (75.93) as he benefits from a significant platoon advantage against the lefty P\u00e9rez and a strong park factor adjustment. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on the most exploitable matchup of the day; facing a struggling Scherzer (5.89 xERA) allows him to leverage his dynamic platoon edge, pushing his score to an impressive 74.56.\n\nOur commitment to aggressive baserunning remains a priority, exemplified by the start of **Nasim Nunez** (64.58). Despite his lower spot in the order, his ability to exploit Scherzer\u2019s slow delivery ensures he remains a primary driver for our stolen base category. The most difficult decision on the bench involved **Miguel Vargas**, who sits at 51.45. While his xwOBA remains high, the optimizer favored **Curtis Mead** (55.09) and **Drake Baldwin** (61.71) for their superior situational platoon and park-adjusted profiles. We are closely monitoring the environment for **Heliot Ramos**, whose score of 56.71 is suppressed slightly by an elite hold pitcher in Sproat; he remains a fringe start today as we keep our cap management in mind. We have avoided exposure to **Liam Hicks** entirely, as his matchup against the elite Wheeler (2.91 xERA) dropped his efficiency well below our 40.0 floor, ensuring we preserve our game counts for more favorable opportunities later in the week.",
